# DELIBERATELY INERT. Every rule below is commented out, so this file assigns
# no owners and GitHub requests review from nobody. The rules are kept verbatim,
# in order, so re-enabling is mechanical rather than a rewrite:
#
#     sed -i 's/^#= //' .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# Re-enable when governance settles -- specifically, when there is a second
# active reviewer and rulesets A and B are being moved off "evaluate". Both
# already carry "require_code_owner_review": true, so they and this file are
# meant to be turned on together; see .github/rulesets/README.md's staged path.
#
# WHY IT IS OFF, and the belief that has to go with it:
#
# This file used to say it "has no effect unless Require review from Code Owners
# is enabled on a ruleset." That is not true, and acting on it cost a
# maintainer's attention. GitHub requests review from code owners when a
# non-draft PR opens against a base branch carrying this file. It does that on
# its own, independent of any ruleset, and independent of enforcement mode --
# every ruleset here is still "evaluate" and blocking nothing. On 2026-08-09 an
# agent opened a PR touching /project-seed/, /.github/workflows/ and
# /.github/rulesets/, named no reviewer, and @mrharpo was requested anyway. The
# notification cannot be recalled.
#
# So this file is not dormant configuration waiting on a ruleset. It is live the
# moment it exists, and it was live while the corpus's own documentation said it
# was not. Until code-owner review is something the org actually wants to field,
# inert is the honest state.
#
# The catch-all below names four people, so the blast radius is not limited to
# the paths an agent is working in. It is currently smaller than it looks only
# because GitHub silently skips users without write access -- that is an
# accident of permissions, not a design, and it grows as access is granted.
#
# Drafts remain the first line of defence regardless: a draft PR fires none of
# this even with the rules live. See AGENTS.md rule 3.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ratification is a human action (README.md, "Ratification"). This file names
# which humans, per path. Tool involvement is never a byline.
#
# GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from the PR's BASE branch, so a project/* branch does
# not get code-owner review until main has been propagated into it.

#= *                       @subcontrabass @mrharpo @CameronRWest @MJWKagstrom

# The ratification surface: Status flips, number assignment, the index.
#= /records/               @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /README.md              @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /PRINCIPLES.md          @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /TEMPLATE.md            @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# The seed is copied verbatim into every fork, so an error here replicates
# into repositories this corpus does not govern.
#= /project-seed/          @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# Enforcement: a PR must not weaken the checks that gate it.
#= /.github/workflows/     @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /.github/CODEOWNERS     @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /.github/rulesets/      @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# Licensing: the outbound grant and the texts it refers to.
#= /LICENSE                @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /LICENSES/              @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /REUSE.toml             @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# Explicitly unowned: non-binding by construction, and gated on merge to main
# by the ruleset rather than by per-path ownership.
#= /perspectives/
#= /math/
